@!internal

--- The blocking-work pool under the native core's reactor: the host's fixed
--- set of threads that make the file system calls readiness cannot wait for
--- (open, read and write on regular files), running no Nupp code. A call of
--- one is the core's own library call, and requiring this module loads
--- nothing: it exists only on the core, for `nupp.runtime.reactor`. A job's
--- bytes are copied in when it is submitted and out when it is collected.
local record poolcalls
    --- Starts `threads` workers, once: the wake descriptor, readable while
    --- finished jobs wait to be taken. Later calls answer the same one.
    start: function(threads: integer): integer

    --- Submits an open of the file at `path` with the access `flags` asks for,
    --- as `filecalls.open` takes them: its ticket.
    open: function(path: string, flags: integer): integer

    --- Submits a read of at most `count` bytes from `descriptor`: its ticket.
    read: function(descriptor: integer, count: integer): integer

    --- Submits a write of `text` from its byte `first` to `descriptor`: its
    --- ticket.
    write: function(descriptor: integer, text: string, first: integer): integer

    --- The ticket of a finished job not yet taken, oldest first, or 0.
    take: function(): integer

    --- Collects the taken job `ticket`, spending it: for a read (`room` at
    --- least 0) the bytes it read, at most `room`; otherwise (`room` -1) the
    --- descriptor or count its system call answered. Either way a failure
    --- is the negated error number.
    finish: function(ticket: integer, room: integer): string | integer

    --- Withdraws job `ticket` if no worker has started it: 1, and the ticket
    --- is spent; 0, and it is still to be taken and collected.
    cancel: function(ticket: integer): integer
end

local calls: poolcalls
return calls
